## Yellow Gold vs White Gold vs Platinum vs Rose Gold

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Metal</th><th>Colour Grade Minimum</th><th>Price Premium</th><th>Lifetime Durability</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>14k Yellow Gold</strong></td><td>H–J</td><td>Baseline</td><td>15–20 years</td><td>Our pick for budget + warmth.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>18k Yellow Gold</strong></td><td>H–J</td><td>+$200–$400</td><td>20–25 years</td><td>Richer colour, slightly softer.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>14k Rose Gold</strong></td><td>H–I</td><td>Baseline</td><td>15–20 years</td><td>Pink warmth. See <a href="/rose-gold-marquise-engagement-ring">rose gold guide</a>.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>14k White Gold</strong></td><td>F–G</td><td>Baseline (rhodium wear)</td><td>15–20 years + rhodium re-plate</td><td>Classic cool. See <a href="/white-gold-marquise-engagement-ring">white gold guide</a>.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Platinum</strong></td><td>F–G</td><td>+$300–$600</td><td>50+ years</td><td>Lifetime metal. Highest colour sensitivity.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** Yellow gold allows the lowest colour grade of any marquise metal — H-J range. White gold and platinum demand F-G minimum. For buyers prioritising stone savings over metal "status," yellow gold is the honest answer. For buyers who want lifetime metal, platinum regardless of colour-grade premium.

